<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Salamanca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1218">1218</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salamanca">Salamanca</a> is the oldest university in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> still operating, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-ix-of-leon">Alfonso IX of León</a> in 1218 and granted a royal charter in 1254. In the sixteenth century it was one of the leading universities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-vitoria">Francisco de Vitoria</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/school-of-salamanca">School of Salamanca</a> developed ideas on natural law, the rights of peoples and economics that influenced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-law">international law</a>. The old city of Salamanca is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-salamanca.jpg" alt="University of Salamanca" width="320" height="460" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:University_of_Salamanca.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
